# ui/glyph (id 129): draw or measure a 0-terminated text run, one unit per word (v2, block ops).
# Args: P0 buffer address, T0 pen x, T1 top y, T2 colour, T3 clip right (last x allowed),
# T8 meas (1 = measure), T9 background colour (drawn behind ink in each glyph row).
# This step block-reads 64 units at P0 (K = 64, N = 64) and enters glrow (175) with
# T5 = 0 (unit index) and T6 = -1 (start of a character). glrow returns to (LR, LP) with
# T0 = pen after the last glyph (measure: start + width).
# Note: weights/ui/glyph.md (derivation, font format). The font ROM is in glrow.wt.
input 65
slice 0 26 27                     # v1 = [P0]
dense 1 7 1                       # v2 = words 0..6
   0
   0
   1                              # addr = P0
   0
   0
   0
   0
   175 4 0 67108928 0 0 0         # next glrow, mem_op 4 block read, value = 64 2^20 + 64
slice 0 8 35                      # v3 = words 7..33 pass
dense 1 2 1                       # v4 = T5 = 0, T6 = -1
   0
   0
   0 -1
slice 0 37 65                     # v5 = words 36..63 pass
concat 2 3
concat 6 4
concat 7 5                        # v8 = output (64)
